### Source-native document structure

In v2, `documentMetadata` and `documentOutline` are required on every `PolicyDocument` and `QuoteDocument`. This is a breaking schema change from v1: hosts should persist both fields and render `documentOutline` as the primary policy breakdown whenever it is non-empty.

`documentOutline` preserves the original document hierarchy and order. Use SDK labels such as `type`, `label`, and `interpretationLabels` as interpretation hints only; do not regroup the document into application-owned buckets such as "strict policy details" or "covered reasons" when rendering the policy text. Extracted facts can carry `documentNodeId`, `sourceSpanIds`, and `sourceTextHash`, which lets a host show the fact inside the original section while still opening the precise source span.

```typescript
interface DocumentMetadata {
  formInventory?: FormReference[];
  tableOfContents?: DocumentTableOfContentsEntry[];
  pageMap?: DocumentPageMapEntry[];
  agentGuidance?: DocumentAgentGuidance[];
}

interface DocumentNode {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  originalTitle?: string;
  type?: string;
  label?: string;
  level?: number;
  sectionNumber?: string;
  pageStart?: number;
  pageEnd?: number;
  formNumber?: string;
  formTitle?: string;
  excerpt?: string;
  content?: string;
  interpretationLabels?: string[];
  sourceSpanIds?: string[];
  sourceTextHash?: string;
  children?: DocumentNode[];
}
```

