    retroactiveDate?: string;
    formNumber?: string;
    sectionRef?: string;
    endorsementNumber?: string;
    limits: OperationalCoverageTerm[];
    sourceNodeIds: string[];
    sourceSpanIds: string[];
  }>;
  parties: OperationalParty[];
  endorsementSupport: OperationalEndorsementSupport[];
  sourceNodeIds: string[];
  sourceSpanIds: string[];
  warnings: string[];
}
```

`SourceBackedValue.value` preserves the extracted source-backed display value. For party and identity fields such as `namedInsured`, `insurer`, `broker`, and `policyNumber`, `normalizedValue` may contain the display-safe canonical identity after removing label fragments or address/contact tails. The compatibility `InsuranceDocument` projection prefers `normalizedValue` for those identity fields when present, while retaining raw `value` for dates, premium, and other fields where the extracted display format is meaningful.

`PolicyOperationalProfile.parties` is the policy-scoped owner for producer/broker, insurer/carrier, and MGA/administrator information. Party addresses may be partial in the profile; complete named-insured, producer, and insurer addresses are also projected into the compatibility document. `operationsDescription` must be directly supported by policy source IDs.

